### 2. Provider Card Responsiveness
#### [MODIFY] `lib/screens/workers_browse_screen.dart`
- **Fix Stretching:** The current `GridView` uses a fixed `childAspectRatio` which causes cards to stretch unnaturally on web browsers. I will change this to `SliverGridDelegateWithMaxCrossAxisExtent`.
- **Responsive Layout:** This ensures cards maintain a maximum width (e.g., 400px) and wrap elegantly depending on the screen size, preventing the massive, stretched UI shown in your screenshots.

### 3. Remove Mock Workers & Integrate Firestore
#### [MODIFY] `lib/services/auth_service.dart`
- **The Issue:** The app is currently using `SharedPreferences` (local storage) as a placeholder database, which is why Firestore is empty and you see hardcoded workers like "UA" (Usman Ali) and "ZA".
- **The Fix:** I will completely remove the `_seedDemoWorkers()` method so the mock workers disappear. 
- **Firestore Integration:** I will rewrite the core methods in `AuthService` (`register`, `login`, `getAllWorkers`) to actually read and write from your connected Firebase Firestore database (`FirebaseFirestore.instance.collection('users')`). This means real data will now flow into your Firebase console!

### 4. Real-Time AI Agent Simulation
#### [MODIFY] `lib/screens/voice_booking_agent.dart`
- **The Issue:** The agent steps are currently hardcoded to appear all at once instantly.
- **The Fix:** I will introduce asynchronous delays (`await Future.delayed`) between each reasoning step (Intent Parsing -> Demand Checking -> Provider Ranking). This will force the UI to render the steps sequentially, creating a true "real-time" checking experience.

